  "body": "#677, the follow-up to #261 part 2: the drilling refusals that quote a hole now name it, so the viewport marks the hole and the op page's refusal line jumps to it.\n\n**Stacked on #678.** This branch is built on `vilts:issue/261-refused-location`. Because that branch lives in a fork, this PR can't target it, so it targets `main`, and until #678 merges its diff also shows #678's commit (82428410). **Review only the last commit (016d417d).** Once #678 merges, this PR shrinks to that commit. #678 is a `feat` that merges at the cut, so this one merges at the same cut, after it.\n\nFork synced at v0.16.0.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Axial drill (app):** the flute-reach, holder and shank-fit refusals (`drill_reach`) and the R-plane refusal (`drill_top`) mark the hole at the material top their law measured from. When that top is unknown, they use the entry Z.\n- **Cross drill:**\n  - The flute-reach refusal (`cross_reach`, already in world) and the finished-part refusal (`cross_part`) mark the modelled mouth.\n  - The kernel's plunge-axis and bottom-above-entry refusals (`drilling/cross.rs`), and the raw stock's plunge-direction refusal (`cross_stock`), mark the local mouth, which `in_world` carries to world.\n  - `to_raw_mouths` was the one spindle-frame refusal that didn't pass through `in_world`; now it does. Its sentence for an off-origin work offset now quotes the world mouth, like every other cross-hole refusal. Nothing changes on origin.\n- **Lathe axial drill (`drilling/axial.rs`):** the off-axis and wider-than-bore refusals mark the mouth. The past-the-bar-end refusal marks the floor.\n- **Listed sites that name no spot** get a one-line comment saying why:\n  - The stitch fork runs at collect time, in the tilted walk frame, before `run_job` maps frames.\n  - The turning chamfer/taper doors name meridian stations, and there is no meridian-to-world map yet.\n  - The deburr, rotary-height, bore-bar and thread-axis refusals are about a size or an angle, not a place.\n- `drilling/cross.rs` is at 401 lines, from 400. A local closure keeps the change to one line.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/677-refusal-spots.md`.\n\n## How it was tested\n\nPinning tests (existing refusal tests that now also assert the spot):\n- `camcraft-motion` lib:\n  - `drilling::tests_cross::cross_drill_refuses_nonsense_by_name` (a Z plunge marks its mouth)\n  - `drilling::tests_cross::cross_drill_refuses_a_bottom_above_the_mouth`\n- `camcraft-app`:\n  - `drill_rplane::an_r_plane_below_the_unfaced_stock_top_is_refused_by_name`: spot (0, 0, 25), the stock top.\n  - `drill_reach_fit::a_bore_bar_whose_shank_is_wider_than_the_hole_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `drill_reach::a_short_flute_cross_drill_on_raw_stock_wider_than_the_part_is_refused_by_name`: world mouth (10, 0, 0), on lathe and mill-turn.\n  - `drilling_axial::an_off_axis_hole_refuses_by_name`\n  - `drilling_axial::a_hole_past_the_bar_end_refuses_by_name`: the floor.\n\nQuick gate (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -Base 82428410` on the last commit, by a separate gate-runner agent): green.\n- motion: lib plus 10 mapped test binaries, 0 failed.\n- app: lib plus 12 mapped binaries (drill_*, drilling_cross_*, stitch_cross, deburr_links, edge_break_gate), plus drilling_axial, lathe_post_refusals, operations and refusal_location; 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- An off-origin cross drill hitting the raw-stock plunge-direction refusal. The shift is `in_world`'s, which its own unit test (from #678) covers.\n- Located refusals under a 3+2 tilt, same as #678.\n- Nothing in the UI changed; #678 covers the mark and the link.\n\nChangelog: Drilling refusals (flute reach, holder, shank fit, R plane, cross-hole and lathe axial doors) now mark the hole they name in the viewport (#677)\n\nFixes #677\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
